    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d46">

                <pb facs="0147" n="37" sameAs="frus:frus1928v03/pg37"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">868.51 Struma Valley/16: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Greece</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Skinner</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Athens</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-05-14T11:00:00+02:00"><hi rendition="#italic">May 14, 1928—11
                                a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received May 14—10:10
                    a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>39. Government decided Saturday night<anchor n="56" xml:id="d46-f1"/> to grant
                    drainage contract to combination of Ulen and Company and Monks interests and to
                    the Foundation Company. Total expenditure approximately $40,000,000.</p>
                <p>[Paraphrase.] The official pressure by the British on behalf of their firm, Boot
                    and Company, was very strong, but it did not succeed in getting the contract.
                    [End paraphrase.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Skinner</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
